BT /F1 11 Tf 14 TL 40 750 Td (Python Library Documentation: module heapq) Tj T* (NAME) Tj T* (heapq - Heap queue algorithm \(a.k.a. priority queue\).) Tj T* (MODULE REFERENCE) Tj T* (https://docs.python.org/3.14/library/heapq.html) Tj T* (The following documentation is automatically generated from the Python) Tj T* (source files.  It may be incomplete, incorrect or include features that) Tj T* (are considered implementation detail and may vary between Python) Tj T* (implementations.  When in doubt, consult the module reference at the) Tj T* (location listed above.) Tj T* (DESCRIPTION) Tj T* (Heaps are arrays for which a[k] <= a[2*k+1] and a[k] <= a[2*k+2] for) Tj T* (all k, counting elements from 0.  For the sake of comparison,) Tj T* (non-existing elements are considered to be infinite.  The interesting) Tj T* (property of a heap is that a[0] is always its smallest element.) Tj T* (Usage:) Tj T* (heap = []            # creates an empty heap) Tj T* (heappush\(heap, item\) # pushes a new item on the heap) Tj T* (item = heappop\(heap\) # pops the smallest item from the heap) Tj T* (item = heap[0]       # smallest item on the heap without popping it) Tj T* (heapify\(x\)           # transforms list into a heap, in-place, in linear time) Tj T* (item = heappushpop\(heap, item\) # pushes a new item and then returns) Tj T* (# the smallest item; the heap size is unchanged) Tj T* (item = heapreplace\(heap, item\) # pops and returns smallest item, and adds) Tj T* (# new item; the heap size is unchanged) Tj T* (Our API differs from textbook heap algorithms as follows:) Tj T* (- We use 0-based indexing.  This makes the relationship between the) Tj T* (index for a node and the indexes for its children slightly less) Tj T* (obvious, but is more suitable since Python uses 0-based indexing.) Tj T* (- Our heappop\(\) method returns the smallest item, not the largest.) Tj T* (These two make it possible to view the heap as a regular Python list) Tj T* (without surprises: heap[0] is the smallest item, and heap.sort\(\)) Tj T* (maintains the heap invariant!) Tj T* (FUNCTIONS) Tj T* (heapify\(heap, /\)) Tj T* () Tj T* ET
